              "start_seconds": 738,
              "end_seconds": 1230,
              "label": "Create a supplied workflow, trigger it, and inspect step logs",
              "summary": "A Java/Gradle workflow template creates a YAML file under .github/workflows. Its event section specifies pushes to the master branch and pull requests targeting that branch. A job groups steps: uses invokes reusable actions for checking out the repository and preparing Java, while run executes supplied commands. The example requires an existing Java/Gradle application. Creating a pull request triggers the workflow, and opening its execution details reveals the completed steps. The logs distinguish executed commands from their output and show setup, checkout, Java preparation, a successful build, and automatic cleanup. These execution details establish what actually ran; the workflow declaration alone does not establish success.",
              "fact_ids": [
                "f1",
                "f3"
              ],
              "transcript_ref": "R8_veQiYBjI:738-1230"
            }
          ],
          "group_title": "From workflow YAML to execution evidence",
          "bridge": {
            "before": "Watch how the supplied template connects triggering events to a job, then follow that execution into step logs. Treat the application and commands as supplied inputs.",
            "after": "The clip explains jobs and uses/run steps but does not explain runs-on runner selection. The text supplies that missing link between the job and its runner."
          },
          "default_mode": "video"
        }
      ]
